.TH CLAUDE-SESSION 1 "2026-07-27" "claude-session 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-session \- launch/attach Claude Code sessions in tmux, with multi-account
support, chat transfer, scheduling, and a doctor view
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-session
.RI [ project ]
.RI [ new | N ]
.br
.B claude-session
.RI [ verb ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude-session
launches or attaches a Claude Code session inside
.BR tmux (1),
so it survives SSH or editor-tunnel disconnects. It provides state-aware
duplicate detection, multiple isolated Claude Code accounts, chat title
tracking, a
.B doctor
view for stuck or orphaned processes, on-disk chat transfer between accounts,
and prompt scheduling via the platform's user-level scheduler.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B claude-session
Project is the current directory's basename; attaches to (or creates)
session \fI<project>\fR-claude.
.TP
.BI "claude-session " project
Attach to (or create) session \fI<project>\fR-claude.
.TP
.BI "claude-session " project " new"
Next free \fI<project>\fR-claude-\fIN\fR.
.TP
.BI "claude-session " project " " N
Specific \fI<project>\fR-claude-\fIN\fR.
.TP
.B claude-session new
From inside \fI~/<project>\fR, next free numbered session.
.TP
.B claude-session ls
List sessions: numbered cards and chat titles, no picker.
.TP
.B claude-session resume
Interactive picker: choose a chat to open or preview (uses
.BR fzf (1)
if present).
.TP
.B claude-session doctor
Find duplicate sessions, stalls, dead session files, orphaned dev processes
(ppid=1), and stuck builds.
.TP
.B claude-session doctor --reap [--force]
Kill the orphaned dev processes found by
.BR doctor .
Confirms interactively unless
.BR --force .
.TP
.B claude-session kill
Interactive: pick session(s) to kill, shows RAM usage.
.TP
.BI "claude-session kill " session
Direct
.B tmux kill-session
shortcut.
.TP
.BI "claude-session accounts add " name " [description]"
Register a new account and run an interactive
.B /login
under it.
.TP
.B claude-session accounts ls
List registered accounts.
.TP
.BI "claude-session accounts rm " name
Unregister an account (credentials are left on disk).
.TP
.BI "claude-session " "native-claude-args"
Runs native
.BR claude (1)
pass-through: inline (exec) for one-shot verbs like \fBupdate\fR/\fBmcp\fR,
tmux for interactive ones like \fB--resume\fR.
.TP
.BI "claude-session -- " args
Forces native routing, for verbs that clash with claude-session's own
(e.g. \fB-- doctor\fR). Both forms honor \fB--account=\fR.
.TP
.BI "claude-session transfer " "[sessionId]" " --to=" account " [--from=" account "] [--move] [--force] [--limit=" N "] [--launch]"
Copy (or, with \fB--move\fR, move) one chat's on-disk state between accounts.
Omit \fIsessionId\fR to pick from the source account's chats across every
project (50 most recent by default; \fB--limit=0\fR for all). Pure data
operation; never touches tmux. \fB--launch\fR reopens the moved chat, resumed,
under the destination account.
.TP
.BI "claude-session transfer log " "[--from=A --to=B --sid=S --since=DATE --limit=N]"
Show the transfer history (ledger).
.TP
.BI "claude-session transfer undo " "[sid|id]"
Reverse the last (or a named) transfer.
.TP
.BI "claude-session transfer redo " id
Re-apply a logged transfer.
.TP
.BI "claude-session transfer prune " id
Drop a ledger record (keeps the chat data).
.TP
.BI "claude-session schedule add " prompt " (--chat=" sid "|--new) (--every=" dur "|--daily-at=" HH:MM "|--once=\(dqYYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\(dq) [--account=] [--mode=plan|autopilot] [--cwd=] [--timeout=]"
Schedule a prompt via the platform scheduler (systemd user timer on Linux,
launchd on macOS).
.TP
.BI "claude-session schedule ls|log " id "|rm " id "|run " id
List, inspect, remove, or fire a scheduled prompt.
.TP
.BI "claude-session schedule keepalive " "[--account=NAME|--all-accounts] [--every=" dur "] [--at=" HH:MM "|--in=" dur "]"
Create (idempotently) a self-pinging low-cost schedule per account, to keep
its 5-hour usage window warm. Details:
.IR docs/keepalive.md
in the source distribution.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --force ", " -f
Override the "already RC-bridged" guard; for \fBtransfer\fR, allow
overwriting at the destination.
.TP
.BI --to= NAME
Transfer destination account (required by \fBtransfer\fR).
.TP
.BI --from= NAME
Transfer source account (default: the default account).
.TP
.B --move
Transfer removes the source copy instead of keeping it.
.TP
.BI --limit= N
Transfer picker: how many recent chats to list (0 = all).
.TP
.BR --plain ", " -p
Force non-interactive mode (no picker even in \fBresume\fR).
.TP
.B --reap
With \fBdoctor\fR: kill orphaned dev processes (ppid=1); needs a TTY confirm
or \fB--force\fR.
.TP
.BI --handoff= FILE
Read \fIFILE\fR as initial takeover context (any agent's handoff).
.TP
.BI --mode= MODE
\fBinteractive\fR, \fBplan\fR, or \fBautopilot\fR (maps to
\fB--permission-mode\fR).
.TP
.BI --account= NAME
Run under a registered account's isolated \fBCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\fR (session
becomes \fI<project>\fR-claude-\fINAME\fR); omit for the default account.
.TP
.B --all-accounts
With \fBschedule keepalive\fR: create the keepalive schedule for every
registered account (default account included) instead of just one.
.TP
.BI --at= HH:MM
With \fBschedule keepalive\fR: anchor the first fire to this clock time
(24h, e.g. an account's known 5-hour usage-window reset) instead of firing
one minute after creation. Single-account only; ignored (with a warning)
under \fB--all-accounts\fR, since every account resets at a different time.
.TP
.BI --in= DURATION
With \fBschedule keepalive\fR: anchor the first fire this far in the future
(a systemd span like \fB3h\fR) instead of one minute after creation.
Single-account only, same caveat as \fB--at\fR.
.TP
.B --version
Print the claude-session version, platform, bash version, resolved library
directory, and the native \fBclaude\fR version. Use
\fBclaude-session -- --version\fR for Claude Code's own version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/claude-helpers/accounts.conf
Registered account list (bash-sourced, one \fBaccount\fR call per line).
.TP
.I ~/.config/claude-helpers/transfer-log.jsonl
The transfer ledger: one JSON object per line, one line per
\fBtransfer\fR/\fBundo\fR/\fBredo\fR event. Overridable via
\fBLEDGER_FILE\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/claude-helpers/schedules/
One subdirectory per scheduled prompt (\fImeta\fR and \fIprompt.txt\fR).
Overridable via \fBSCHED_DIR\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/claude-schedule-*.{service,timer}
Generated systemd user units backing each schedule on Linux. Overridable via
\fBSYSTEMD_USER_DIR\fR.
.TP
.I <config-dir>/sessions/*.json
Live per-process session state Claude Code itself writes; \fIconfig-dir\fR
is \fI~/.claude\fR for the default account, or the directory registered for
a named account.
.TP
.I <config-dir>/projects/*/*.jsonl
Chat transcripts — what \fBtransfer\fR copies or moves between accounts.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Overrides the active account's Claude Code config directory; set
automatically by \fB--account=\fR, but can also be set directly by callers
that want to run one-off commands under a specific account.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_HELPERS_LIB
Overrides the resolved library directory (normally found relative to
\fBbin/claude-session\fR's own, symlink-followed location). Set this if the
library files live somewhere \fBclaude-session\fR cannot infer.
.TP
.B LEDGER_FILE
Overrides the transfer ledger path (default
\fI~/.config/claude-helpers/transfer-log.jsonl\fR).
.TP
.B SCHED_DIR
Overrides the schedules directory (default
\fI~/.config/claude-helpers/schedules\fR).
.TP
.B SYSTEMD_USER_DIR
Overrides where generated systemd user units are written (default
\fI~/.config/systemd/user\fR).
.TP
.B ORPHAN_PS_SRC
When set, points \fBdoctor\fR's process-table scan at a fixture file instead
of the real process table — used by the test suite for hermetic, host-
independent orphan/stuck-build detection. Also forces \fBdoctor --reap\fR
into a dry run, since fixture pids are arbitrary numbers that could
coincide with real, live pids on the host running the test.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_COMPAT_OS
Overrides platform detection (\fBlinux\fR or \fBdarwin\fR) in the
compatibility layer; used by tests to exercise both branches from one host.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime error: missing dependency, unreadable file, unknown account, a
failed ledger write, or similar.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage: a required flag was missing (e.g. \fBtransfer\fR without
\fB--to=\fR), an argument failed validation (e.g. a malformed
\fB--every=\fR span), or \fBdoctor --reap\fR was asked to run unattended
without \fB--force\fR on a non-interactive stdin.
.PP
\fBdoctor\fR itself (without \fB--reap\fR) exits with the count of issues
found, so \fB0\fR also means "all clear" there specifically.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Attach to (or start) the current directory's session:
.B claude-session
.TP
Start a second, independent session for the same project:
.B claude-session myproject new
.TP
List every session across every account:
.B claude-session ls
.TP
Run the health check, then clean up anything it flagged as reapable:
.B claude-session doctor
.br
.B claude-session doctor --reap
.TP
Register a second account and use it for one project:
.B claude-session accounts add work
.br
.B claude-session myproject --account=work
.TP
Copy the currently-picked chat to another account and reopen it there:
.B claude-session transfer --to=work --launch
.TP
Schedule a daily standup-summary prompt against a fresh chat:
.B claude-session schedule add "Summarize yesterday's commits" --new --daily-at=09:00
.TP
Print claude-session's own version:
.B claude-session --version
.TP
Print Claude Code's own version instead:
.B claude-session -- --version
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR claude (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR systemd.timer (5),
.BR launchd.plist (5)
